Project Proposal: Fast Food Restaurants in Germany

Introduction
Fast food chains like McDonald's, Burger King, and Subway are everywhere in Germany, but they're not spread out evenly. Some cities have dozens of locations, while others have very few. This project looks at where these restaurants are located and tries to find patterns across cities and states.

Problem Statement
It's not clear why some cities and states have more fast food restaurants than others. This project will look at restaurant locations across Germany to find out which areas have the most and least, and which chains show up most often.

What Data I'm Using
●	Restaurant name and chain
●	City and address
●	State (Bundesland)
●	Location coordinates (latitude/longitude)

Questions I Want to Answer
●	Which cities have the most and least fast food restaurants?
●	Which cities have the most McDonald's per person?
●	Which states have the highest and lowest number of restaurants per person?
●	Which chain has the most locations overall?
●	How do big cities like Berlin, Hamburg, and Munich compare to smaller towns?

How I'll Do It
1. Collect the restaurant data and clean it up.
2. Add population numbers for each city and state so I can compare fairly.
3. Count and rank restaurants by city, state, and chain.
4. Make charts and a short summary of what I find.

Tools
Power BI for the analysis and visualization, with data from OpenStreetMap (restaurant locations) and Destatis (German population data).

What I Expect to Find
A clear picture of which parts of Germany have the most fast food restaurants, which chains dominate, and how city size affects how many restaurants an area has.
